    ∃ (K : Type w) (_ : Field K) (_ : Algebra k K)
      (Q : PrimeSpectrum (A ⊗[k] K)) (xK yK : Localization.AtPrime Q.asIdeal),
      xK * yK = 0 ∧ xK ≠ 0 ∧ yK ≠ 0 := by
  -- Route correction: the imported prefix already registers the tensor product with an
  -- integrally closed domain as a normal ring failed: before the main theorem is available,
  -- instance search has no dependency-closed proof of `IsNormalRing (A ⊗[k] C)`. The remaining
  -- source step is the finite-support descent to a residue-field tensor prime. The generic
  -- localization and prime-separation parts of that descent are now isolated in the helpers above.
  -- TODO: represent `x`, `y`, and `hxy` at a finitely generated right subalgebra, then choose a
  -- residue-field prime where their nonzero zero-product survives and transport it to
  -- `A ⊗[k] K`.
